Secondary-CPU progress marks + panic diagnostics (where does CPU1 die?).

0135/0137 fixed the reset; 0141 enabled the SMP validation.  Booting 0141 with
`cpus=4` PSCI CPU_ON for cpu1 returned rc=0, but CPU1 never cleared
SIGPdisabled and the boot panicked:

  SWEET CPU: cpu=1 startup timeout (reset/MMU/GIC/SGI)

Nothing survived (SWEETLOG flusher and the PE_halt_restart hook start later),
so there is no way to tell whether CPU1 reached sweet_secondary_entry,
LowResetVectorBase or initCPU.

0142 records the secondary path's progress in fixed globals and prints it in
the timeout panic:

  sweet_secondary_marks[8]  per logical CPU (index = PSCI context / MPIDR):
      1    first instruction of sweet_secondary_entry
      0x12 firmware entered the secondary at EL2
      2    EL1 path, just before `b LowResetVectorBase`
      3    reset_vector reached (VBAR installed)
      4    start_cpu reached, just before `b common_start`
      5    SweetCPU::initCPU first line
      6    after signalCPU() (self-IPI queued)
      7    after initialized = 1
  sweet_smp_stage           last start.s stage any secondary reached:
      0xE0 entry, 0xE2 EL2, 0xE3 EL1, 0xE4 reset_vector, 0xE5 CpuData found,
      0xE6 CpuData/handler not found, 0xE7 before blr handler, 0xE8 start_cpu,
      0xF0 initCPU entered (C side)
      0xEA common_start, 0xEB bootstrap page tables built, 0xEC before SCTLR
      (MMU enable), 0xED MMU on, 0xEE arm_init_tramp returning to arm_init_cpu,
      0xEF unexpected EL
  sweet_smp_vector_hit      early EL1-SP1 exception stub hit (0xF1..0xF4)

The assembly writes work with the MMU off: the kernel image is linked V=P, so
PA(symbol) = PC_pa + (symbol_VA - entry_VA), computed with adr/adrp+add (no
absolute constants).  Every write is followed by `dsb sy`.

The panic and the "NOT alive after 5s" IOLog now print for the failing CPU:
  cpu=%u start phys=0x%x mark=0x%llx stage=0x%llx vec=0x%llx init=%u sig=%u
plus the elapsed ticks, so one photo tells where CPU1 stopped.

Also verified in the plan: the secondary SCTLR value 0x30d00800 is exactly the
ARMv8.0 SCTLR_EL1 RES1 set (bits 11,20,22,23,28,29 - Linux SCTLR_EL1_RES1)
with M/C/I off, and the secondary page-table rebuild uses the same
ARM_TT_Lx_SHIFT/PGBYTES macros as the (working) boot path, no 16K assumption.

Base = post-0141 CI main (xnu-buildtree artifact of run 43216360057).
